hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"126","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, a man at Mina who was beside Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me; I asked Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr about him and he said: This is so-and-so son of 'Abdullah ibn Zayd - the caller of the adhan. I asked that man and he told me from his father that 'Abdullah ibn Zayd gave a walled garden of his in charity. His parents came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing sustained us but it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned it to his parents, then they died and he inherited it from them afterwards."
"127","'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ja'far, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade harvesting by night and cutting dates by night."
"128","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from 'Ali ibn al-Husayn, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade harvesting by night, cutting dates by night, and reaping by night; that was because a caretaker of his cut dates by night."
"129","'Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Naysaburi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi informed us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ja'far, with its chain, likewise. Ja'far said: We think he disliked that only because the poor and needy do not witness it."
"130","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from 'Udhafir al-Basri, from al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever pays the zakah of his wealth has fulfilled the duty upon him, and whoever adds is better."
"131","Muhammad ibn 'Awf al-Ta'i narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Musa ibn Sulayman narrated to me, I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever earns wealth through sin, then joins kinship with it, gives it in charity, or spends it in the path of Allah, all of it will be gathered together and cast with him into Hell."
"132","Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, Abu Nawfal - meaning Ibn Abi 'Aqrab - narrated to us, he said: 'A'ishah said: O Messenger of Allah, where is 'Abdullah ibn Jud'an? He said: In the Fire. She said: It weighed heavily upon her. He said: O 'A'ishah, what weighed heavily upon you? She said: He used to feed food and join kinship. He said: It will be lightened for him because of what you mention."
